Package: mediaPlanR
Type: Package
Title: Reliable Cross-Media Reach and Frequency Planning
Version: 2.0.0
Date: 2026-10-08
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Manuel J.", family = "Sánchez-Franco",
           email = "majesus@us.es", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8042-3550"))
Description: Reproducible tools for cross-media reach and exposure-frequency
    planning. Provides a validated media-plan data contract; exact reach and
    exposure distributions under random duplication (Sainsbury and Binomial
    models); the Beta-Binomial accumulation model and its multi-vehicle
    version of Metheringham (1964) <doi:10.1080/00218499.1964.12519751>; the
    ad hoc duplication and accumulation formulas of Agostini (1961)
    <doi:10.1080/00218499.1961.12519620> and Hofmans (1966)
    <doi:10.1177/002224376600300307>; and the multivariate exposure
    distribution models of Danaher (1991) <doi:10.1177/002224379102800311>
    (canonical expansion), Leckenby and Rice (1986)
    <doi:10.1080/00913367.1986.10673014> (Morgensztern sequential
    aggregation), Hyo Gyoo Kim (2005) (canonical sequential aggregation),
    Heejin Kim (1994)
    (conditional Beta distribution), and Cheong (2007) and Cheong, Leckenby and
    Eakin (2011) <doi:10.2753/JOA0091-3367400101> (multivariate
    Beta-Binomial). Also includes target-audience metrics, an explicitly
    scoped Negative-Binomial count approximation, and budget-constrained
    optimization of effective reach that reports whether a global optimum was
    verified.
